Why AGPL: PDF to Word uses pdf2docx, which depends on PyMuPDF (AGPL-3.0).
When you run this as a public website, the AGPL requires you to offer visitors
the source code of the version you run. Set SOURCE_URL in .env to your public
repository and the site shows a "Source code" link in the footer.

Bundled third-party files:
  web/vendor/pdf.min.mjs, pdf.worker.min.mjs   pdf.js, Apache-2.0 (web/vendor/PDFJS-LICENSE.txt)
  web/fonts/archivo-*.woff2                    Archivo, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (web/fonts/ARCHIVO-LICENSE.txt)
  app/fonts/*.ttf, web/fonts/DejaVu*.ttf       DejaVu fonts, free licence (app/fonts/DEJAVU-LICENSE.txt)
